*** Test Cases ***
CB009019-A2b_1_Online_modification_of_udpMaxDatagramSize_when_TCP_MSS_Clamping_is_enabled
    [Tags]    CRT
    [Documentation]    This test verifies that online modification of udpMaxDatagramSize parameter
    ...                while TCP MSS Clamping is enabled causes change of TCP MSS value on new bearer.
    Set feature flag act5gUserLayerTcpMssClamping to true
    Set feature flag udpMaxDatagramSize to 1400
    Register UE  UE_ID=1  CELL_ID=1
    Establish PDU session  UE_ID=1
    Set feature flag udpMaxDatagramSize to 1200
    Start tshark
    ...   log_filename=any.pcap
    ...   eth_interface=any
    ...   log_dirpath=${OUTPUT_DIR}/${TEST_NAME}
    ...   alias=tcp_mss
    Start 5 mbps DL data traffic on PDU1 for UE1
    Establish PDU session  UE_ID=1  PDU_ID=2  GW_ID=2
    Start 5 mbps DL data traffic on PDU2 for UE1
    Stop capturing  alias=tcp_mss
    Run Keyword And Continue On Failure  Verify value of MSS in TCP [SYN] packet  MSS=1337  source=72.23.0.1  destination=10.0.2.1
    Run Keyword And Continue On Failure  Verify value of MSS in TCP [SYN,ACK] packet  MSS=1336  source=1.2.4.2  destination=10.0.2.1
    Run Keyword And Continue On Failure  Verify value of MSS in TCP [SYN] packet  MSS=1137  source=72.24.0.1  destination=10.0.2.1
    Run Keyword And Continue On Failure  Verify value of MSS in TCP [SYN,ACK] packet  MSS=1136  source=1.2.4.3  destination=10.0.2.1
    Setup.Produce Scout Data
    [Teardown]    Deregister UE1 and clear up test environment
